---
import Feature from '../../components/Feature.astro'
import Snapshot from '../../components/Snapshot.astro'
import Specimen from '../../components/Specimen.astro'
import { FEATURES } from '../../features'
import FeaturePage from '../../layouts/FeaturePage.astro'
import type { PageMeta } from '../../meta'

export const meta = {
  description: FEATURES.review.sentence,
  sources: [
    'docs/github-integration.md',
    'docs/github-integration/surfaces.md',
    'docs/github-integration/reads-and-writes.md',
    'docs/github-integration/mirror.md',
    'docs/diff-rendering.md',
    'docs/diff-rendering/geometry.md',
    'docs/diff-rendering/loading.md',
    'docs/diff-rendering/review.md',
    'docs/diff-rendering/changes-pane.md',
    'docs/git-client/history.md',
    'docs/git-client/operations.md',
    'docs/git-client/stashes.md',
    'docs/git-client/conflicts.md',
    'docs/git-client/explanations.md',
    'docs/first-party-plugins/terminal.md',
    'docs/tui/plugin-losses.md',
    'packages/change-request-ui/src/views/Overview.tsx',
    'packages/change-request-ui/src/views/sections.tsx',
    'packages/change-request-ui/src/views/ChecksPanel.tsx',
  ],
  checked: '70489f534',
} satisfies PageMeta
---

<FeaturePage feature="review" meta={meta} related={['tasks', 'agents', 'automation']} docs={{ href: '/docs/built-in-plugins/github/', label: 'Read about GitHub' }}>
  <Snapshot slot="picture" id="review" />

  <Feature number={1} title="The pull request, inside its task" href="/docs/built-in-plugins/github/" link="GitHub">
    <p>
      Connect GitHub and a task's pull request opens in its own pane: the state, reviewers, labels, linked issues,
      and description, then the conversation as a timeline of comments, reviews, commits, and file threads, beside
      the diff. Comment, review, and request reviewers from the same pane. The GitHub source in the rail lists a
      repository's pull requests, and makes a task from one.
    </p>
  </Feature>

  <Feature number={2} title="Checks, their logs, and re-runs" href="/docs/built-in-plugins/github/" link="GitHub">
    <p>
      Each check sits in the overview with its status. Press one to open its GitHub Actions job, with the failed
      steps open and each step's log under it. A failed check has a <strong>Re-run</strong> button.
    </p>
  </Feature>

  <Feature number={3} title="Merge from the pane" href="/docs/built-in-plugins/github/" link="GitHub">
    <p>
      <strong>Merge</strong> sits beside its method: squash, a merge commit, or rebase. A draft offers{' '}
      <strong>Ready for review</strong> instead, and <strong>Convert to draft</strong> and <strong>Close</strong>{' '}
      sit under it.
    </p>
    <Specimen slot="picture" id="ship" />
  </Feature>

  <Feature number={4} title="A diff viewer for big changes" href="/docs/built-in-plugins/git/" link="Git">
    <p>
      The pull request, the compare view, and the Changes tab share one diff viewer. Read it unified or split, with
      the changed words marked inside each changed line and review threads under the lines they're on. Filter files
      by name and mark them viewed. Viewed marks stay in acorn and aren't sent to GitHub. The viewer loads a diff a
      segment at a time, and reads a pull request up to GitHub's 3,000-file limit.
    </p>
  </Feature>

  <Feature number={5} title="Stage, commit, and push in the task" href="/docs/built-in-plugins/git/" link="Git">
    <p>
      The task's Git pane opens on <strong>Changes</strong>: every changed file stacked in one list, a checkbox to
      stage each file or group, and a commit box. One button pushes, pulls, fetches, or publishes the branch,
      whichever its state calls for. <strong>History</strong>, <strong>Stashes</strong>, and{' '}
      <strong>Worktrees</strong> sit beside it, and <strong>Explain commit</strong> asks a model to summarize the
      commit you selected.
    </p>
  </Feature>

  <Feature number={6} title="Merge, rebase, and resolve a conflict" href="/docs/built-in-plugins/git/" link="Git">
    <p>
      From a commit or a branch, merge it into the task, rebase the task onto it, cherry-pick it, or revert it. acorn
      refuses while the checkout has uncommitted changes or an agent is working in it. A conflicted file opens with
      its base, ours, and theirs beside an editable result, labeled with what each side is, and{' '}
      <strong>Save and stage</strong> writes the result and stages it.
    </p>
  </Feature>

  <Fragment slot="terminal">
    <p>
      The pull request pane, the Git pane, and the diff draw in the terminal client too, with other plugins' marks on
      diff lines. The conflict result is a text area there instead of an editor. GitHub's changed-file and pull request
      searches need the desktop app.{' '}
      <a href="/docs/start/desktop-and-terminal/">Desktop and terminal</a>
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</FeaturePage>
